        "note": "Mathlib's Hadamard matrices over a star ring (Matrix.IsHadamard: unitary entries, orthogonal rows), which over the complex numbers include complex Hadamard matrices, with IsHadamard.four_dvd_card (an integer Hadamard matrix of order greater than two has order divisible by four). It has no notion of entries of a fixed root-of-unity order and does not prove Butson's theorem. Not used by this proof.",
